Subtask 4.3: Create Advanced Variable with Regex
Go to Dashboard settings > Variables
Click Add variable
Create a filtered job variable:
Name: filtered_job
Type: Query
Label: Filtered Jobs
Data source: Prometheus
Query: label_values(up, job)
Regex: /.*app.*/
Sort: Alphabetical (asc)
Multi-value: Enable
Include All option: Enable
Click Update and Save dashboard
Subtask 4.4: Add Variable to Panel Query
Edit one of your existing panels
Modify the query to use the new filtered variable:
up{job=~"$filtered_job", environment=~"$environment"}
Update the panel title to: Filtered Services - $filtered_job
Click Apply
Subtask 4.5: Create Constant Variable for Thresholds
Add a new variable:

Name: cpu_threshold
Type: Constant
Label: CPU Threshold
Value: 80
Create a new panel using this threshold:

Query: prometheus_tsdb_head_samples_appended_total > $cpu_threshold
Title: Services Above $cpu_threshold Threshold
Subtask 4.6: Test Variable Refresh Options
Edit the job variable
Change Refresh to On Dashboard Load
Save and reload the dashboard
Notice how variables refresh automatically
Task 5: Advanced Variable Techniques and Troubleshooting
Subtask 5.1: Create Text Box Variable for Custom Filtering
Add a new variable:

Name: custom_filter
Type: Textbox
Label: Custom Filter
Default value: .*
Use this in a panel query:

up{job=~"$job", instance=~"$custom_filter"}
Subtask 5.2: Implement Variable Chaining
Create a dependent variable chain:

Country Variable:

Name: country
Type: Custom
Values: US,EU,ASIA
Region Variable (modify existing):

Query: label_values(up{region=~"${country:regex}"}, region)
This creates a dependency where region options change based on country selection.

Subtask 5.3: Add Variable Validation
Create a validation panel:

Query: count(up{job=~"$job"}) or vector(0)
Title: Selected Jobs Count: $job
Type: Stat panel
This helps users understand their current selection impact.

